  Three functions are included, in omni_extract_bench/values.py and marked there:
  `canonical` (as `_fold_cosmetic`), `unwrap`, and `_drop_datalab_sidecars`. They were
  copied rather than reimplemented so that scores produced here would remain identical to the
  upstream metric on the same inputs.

  `_fold_cosmetic` has since DIVERGED in ONE place, marked `DIVERGENCE FROM UPSTREAM` in the
  source with its evidence: upstream strips leading zeros inside every digit run, which makes
  `INV-007` == `INV-7`, `02000` == `2000`, `06` == `6`, `arXiv:2405.06211v3` ==
  `arXiv:2405.6211v3`, and `wenqifan03@gmail.com` == `wenqifan3@gmail.com`. Padding is how a
  document says which identifier it means, so that fold is not removed here.

  Everything else upstream folds, this folds too, deliberately -- whitespace, commas, hyphens
  and periods from anywhere in a value. That is lenient, and known to be: it merges `5.2.1.5`
  with `5215`. It was kept because measuring all 660 documents against nine vendors showed the
  fold recovers 1,607 value matches, 1,532 of them differing by punctuation alone, while
  crediting no wrong value as right and merging no two gold values with different digits. The
  price is enumerated in tests/test_canon_properties.py ACCEPTED_LENIENCY.

  `unwrap` and `_drop_datalab_sidecars` remain verbatim.

  The full grader was vendored at omni_extract_bench/vendor/longextract_bench/ until these
  three were the only parts still reachable from the scoring path. Nothing else from it is
  used: this repo scores through omni_extract_bench/score.py alone.
